WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.868
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.636
is a Grammy-nominated comedian
and actor

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.371
you know from his sitcom
"George Lopez"

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.440
and his talk show
"Lopez Tonight."

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.078
His new show "Lopez vs. Lopez"
airs Fridays at 8:00 on NBC

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.447
and streams the next day
on Peacock.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:15.548
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.216
-So he knows all this stuff
about me.

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:19.352
I want to know about
his dirty laundry.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.920
-Yeah, he doesn't have any.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.822
He does laundry every day.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.160
I am not his favorite thing
that is white and delicate.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.632
Now, can we please
move past this

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.066
so we can keep having
a nice family weekend?

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:35.634
It would really mean a lot
to me, George.

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.504
-[ Chuckles ]
I bet it would.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.443
-D-Does that mean he'll do it?

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.077
I don't want to lie to you.

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:46.879
So I'm going to go
to the kitchen.

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:49.982
-Please welcome to the show
George Lopez, everybody!

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:52.018
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.018 --> 00:01:00.426 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:08.835 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.002
-Oh, my God.

00:01:10.002 --> 00:01:11.603
-Welcome to the show, George.

00:01:11.603 --> 00:01:12.505
-I've never been here.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:13.940
-I know,
it's the first time here.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.174
I'm so thrilled to have you.

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:17.310
-I've never been here before.
How about that?

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.612
-First time!

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:23.382
I couldn't help but notice as I
was listing your past credits,

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:24.484
you've done a very smart thing.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.985
You've put your name
in the title

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.686
of everything you've ever done.

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:30.222
"George Lopez" sitcom,
"Lopez Tonight,"

00:01:30.222 --> 00:01:33.058
and now "Lopez vs. Lopez."

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:35.527
Well, there was "St. George"
and there was just "Lopez."

00:01:35.527 --> 00:01:39.698
But "Lopez vs. Lopez" is
the title that we're using now.

00:01:39.698 --> 00:01:43.202
Not as shocking to me as it was

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:45.905
in the divorce papers when
I saw it for the first time.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.774
-Right, so it's better
as a sitcom title

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:50.543
than it is in a legal document?

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:54.446
-You know, anything with the
State of California vs. Lopez

00:01:54.446 --> 00:01:55.815
[bleep] I lost.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.884
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.887
-You know, you've been doing
this for so long, I assume --

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:03.656
You know, you've been doing
stand-up you've had your shows.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.825
People must feel like they
know you when they see you.

00:02:06.825 --> 00:02:10.496
-Well, you know,
you would think.

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:12.198
-Uh-huh.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:16.135
-A Grubhub driver came to
my house on a Saturday morning.

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.304
And he looked in the house
past me, he went,

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:21.040
"Oh, I thought that
George Lopez was here."

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.177
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.711
And at that point,
you got to be

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:27.480
[Spanish accent]
"No, señor, he left, he go."

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.082
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.750
"No here.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.352
He no here."

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:34.821
[ Normal voice ] And then
you ever talk to somebody

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.088
with an accent,
and they get the accent?

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:37.957
"He no here.
The guy like, "He no here?"

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.092
I was like, "No."

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:42.761
-People appreciate when you
speak in their accent, I think.

00:02:42.761 --> 00:02:44.330
-I have to say a bad word.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:48.868
But in the elevator, somebody
said, "You look like somebody."

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.403
They never say, like,
"Who do I look like?"

00:02:51.403 --> 00:02:54.641
And the lady said, "You look
like Cheech [bleep] Chong."

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:56.509
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.013
-Wow.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.617
I mean, I might say that
if I was passing someone.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:08.154
But to be in an elevator...

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.122
-Republicans, they're bold, man.

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:11.257
-They're bold.

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.059
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:15.861
Now, that is your --
that is your actual daughter

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:17.930
who is playing the other Lopez
in the title.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:18.931
That's Mayan.

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:20.500
-That's my daughter,
Mayan Lopez.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.368
-That's amazing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.970
And now, to get serious
for a moment,

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.774
this is inspired by the fact
that you two, in real life,

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.675
were estranged for a while.

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:33.313
What was it like for the two of
you to sort of revisit that time

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.681
and to turn it into comedy?

00:03:35.681 --> 00:03:38.217
-Well, Seth, you know...

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:40.352
first, you have to be
a horrible father.

00:03:40.352 --> 00:03:42.188
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.823
That's step one.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:47.927
-And have broken -- And have
broken everyone's heart.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.328
You've lied to everyone.

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:51.464
Never to Congress,
but everyone in my family.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.032
-Yeah.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:57.069
You know, and in therapy,
you're just taking years of it,

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:00.206
just abuse of years, you know.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:03.609
You can never
say anything about me, you know.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:05.544
As hard as therapy was,

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:08.881
it wasn't as cold
as the elevator ride down.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.483
I mean that's, like --

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.184
You're like [Bleep]
It's three floors.

00:04:12.184 --> 00:04:14.553
And it just feels like forever.

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:17.623
But, you know,
I love Mayan so much

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.992
that it is truly the one
relationship in my life

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:24.163
that I'm willing to take
responsibility for and repair,

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:27.033
because it's my only child
and I love her so much.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:31.704
And if NBCUniversal is going to
pay us to work it out, I'm here.

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:32.872
-Yeah.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.040
There you go.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.175
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:38.343 --> 00:04:40.446
If you can figure out
how to get someone else

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.582
to pay for your therapy,
you have been --

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:45.118
you have been in this business
for a long time.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:47.887
When did you know
Mayan was funny?

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:48.988
And do you think she was

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.490
realizing she was funny
at the same time?

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.592
Or do you think it happened
on a different schedule?

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:57.663
-You know, I think, you know,
when kids are not afraid

00:04:57.663 --> 00:04:59.665
to put, like, their finger
in your butt crack,

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:01.267
you're like, "Hey!"

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:03.002
But my...

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:05.504
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.504 --> 00:05:08.174
My ex-wife --

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:10.409
My ex-wife was very bosomy.

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:12.478
And Mayan would put the bra
on her head

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:15.348
and these two pointy things
and she would just go...

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:16.582
You know?

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:19.152
-Yeah, that's when you know
they got it, yeah.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.887
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:22.321
-And she loves
"Saturday Night Live."

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:23.589
She loves you.
She loves Jimmy.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.391
She just loves comedies.
-Yeah.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:27.226
Well, you guys got
a very natural chemistry

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:28.027
on-screen together.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.295
I got a lot more to ask you.

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:31.731
We'll be right back with more
from George Lopez.

